## Context

The current exporter writes six JSON payloads consumed together by the static renderer. Migration needs a recoverable complete website and precise differences, not merely passing unit tests.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

Interrupt a candidate build after one output and assert the accepted complete bundle, country/project routes and downloads are unchanged. Restore a prior bundle and serve it offline with no DVC or network access.

## Actions

Inventory/hash all inputs, row keys and routes at the accepted commit; freeze matching rendering assets and outputs; add separate candidate output location and semantic difference report. Reuse existing browser tests. Measure the 508002-byte ZAF payload and record the 512000-byte constraint. Do not regenerate canonical data during baseline capture.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Baseline pins input and output hashes, headers, row counts and stable routes
- [ ] Candidate failure cannot partially replace accepted files
- [ ] Restoration and offline browser navigation/downloads pass
- [ ] Difference report separates intentional scientific changes from metadata-only differences

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

